---
import type { Locale } from "../../config/site";

interface Props {
  locale: Locale;
}
const { locale } = Astro.props;
const de = locale === "de";
---

<header class="section-heading">
  <div class="brush-heading-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">{de ? "Pinsel-Engines" : "Brush engines"}</p>
    <h2>
      {de
        ? "Jeder Pinsel kann anders programmiert werden."
        : "Each brush can be programmed differently."}
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="brush-intro">
    <p>
      {de
        ? "Ein Pinsel ist nicht bloß ein Stempel aus Texturen. Seine Engine kann mit eigenem Rendering-Code auf Druck, Form, Textur, Farbe, Abstand und Drehung reagieren."
        : "A brush is not merely a stamp made from textures. Its engine can use its own rendering code to respond to pressure, shape, texture, color, spacing, and rotation."}
    </p>
    <p class="brush-formula-note">
      {de
        ? "Dieselben oben beschriebenen Formeln pro Pixel arbeiten auch in jedem Pinsel: Eine kann ein sauberes Polygon formen, eine andere Tinte aufbauen oder Druck in Farbe übersetzen."
        : "The same per-pixel formulas described above live inside each brush: one can shape a clean polygon, while another builds up ink or turns pressure into color."}
    </p>
  </div>
</header>
<div
  class="brush-table"
  aria-label={de ? "Auszüge aus dem Pinsel-Shader" : "Brush shader excerpts"}
>
  <figure>
    <div class="code-card" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="code-card__bar">
        <span>shape.wgsl</span>
        <i></i>
        <i></i>
        <i></i>
      </div>
      <pre><code><span class="syntax-comment">// Hold the short axis at the pixel floor.</span>
<span class="syntax-keyword">fn</span> <span class="syntax-function">squish</span>(amount: <span class="syntax-type">f32</span>) -&gt; <span class="syntax-type">Squish</span> &#123;
  <span class="syntax-keyword">let</span> s = <span class="syntax-function">clamp</span>(amount, -<span class="syntax-number">1.0</span>, <span class="syntax-number">1.0</span>);
  <span class="syntax-keyword">let</span> s2 = s * s;
  <span class="syntax-keyword">let</span> wanted = (<span class="syntax-number">1.0</span> - s2) / (<span class="syntax-number">1.0</span> + s2);

  <span class="syntax-keyword">let</span> scale = <span class="syntax-function">select</span>(
    <span class="syntax-type">vec2&lt;f32&gt;</span>(<span class="syntax-number">1.0</span> / wanted, <span class="syntax-number">1.0</span>),
    <span class="syntax-type">vec2&lt;f32&gt;</span>(<span class="syntax-number">1.0</span>, <span class="syntax-number">1.0</span> / wanted),
    s &lt; <span class="syntax-number">0.0</span>
  );
  <span class="syntax-keyword">return</span> <span class="syntax-type">Squish</span>(scale, <span class="syntax-number">1.0</span>);
&#125;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <figcaption>{de ? "Form · Quetschung" : "Shape · squish"}</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure>
    <div class="code-card" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="code-card__bar">
        <span>shape.wgsl</span>
        <i></i>
        <i></i>
        <i></i>
      </div>
      <pre><code><span class="syntax-comment">// The squished outline, counter-clockwise.</span>
<span class="syntax-keyword">var</span> vertex: <span class="syntax-type">array&lt;vec2&lt;f32&gt;, MAX_SIDES&gt;</span>;

<span class="syntax-keyword">for</span> (<span class="syntax-keyword">var</span> k = <span class="syntax-number">0</span>; k &lt; n; k++) &#123;
  <span class="syntax-keyword">let</span> angle = <span class="syntax-number">2.0</span> * PI * <span class="syntax-type">f32</span>(k)
    / <span class="syntax-type">f32</span>(n);

  vertex[k] = outer * <span class="syntax-type">vec2&lt;f32&gt;</span>(
    <span class="syntax-function">cos</span>(angle),
    <span class="syntax-function">sin</span>(angle)
  ) / squished.scale;
&#125;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <figcaption>{de ? "Polygon · Kanten" : "Polygon · edges"}</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure>
    <div class="code-card" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="code-card__bar">
        <span>shape.wgsl</span>
        <i></i>
        <i></i>
        <i></i>
      </div>
      <pre><code><span class="syntax-comment">// Soften the edge by exactly one screen pixel.</span>
<span class="syntax-keyword">let</span> width = <span class="syntax-function">max</span>(
  band,
  <span class="syntax-function">max</span>(s.screen_pixel, <span class="syntax-number">1e-6</span>)
);
<span class="syntax-keyword">let</span> grow = (width - band) * <span class="syntax-number">0.5</span>;

<span class="syntax-keyword">let</span> coverage = <span class="syntax-number">1.0</span> - <span class="syntax-function">smoothstep</span>(
  -grow,
  band + grow,
  distance
);

<span class="syntax-keyword">return</span> <span class="syntax-type">vec4&lt;f32&gt;</span>(s.ink, coverage * s.strength);</code></pre>
    </div>
    <figcaption>{de ? "Kante · Deckkraft" : "Edge · coverage"}</figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>
<div class="brush-notes">
  <p class="future-note">
    <strong>{de ? "Die Richtung:" : "The direction:"}</strong>{" "}
    {de
      ? "Austauschbare Pakete aus Pinselmodellen, Vorgaben und Texturen. Noch nicht zum Download verfügbar."
      : "Exchangeable packs of brush models, presets, and textures. Not available to download yet."}
  </p>
  <p class="scope-note">
    <strong>{de ? "Bewusster Fokus:" : "A deliberate focus:"}</strong>{" "}
    {de
      ? "Das geplante nasse Malen soll Farben überzeugend auf der Leinwand mischen. Es ist kein Versprechen, jede physikalische Eigenschaft echter Farbe zu simulieren."
      : "The planned wet-painting tool is intended to mix colors convincingly on the canvas. It is not a promise to simulate every physical property of real paint."}
  </p>
</div>
